      "width": 831.6,
      "height": 135,
      "text": "For each request, write down the exact status + body the client gets\nand which handlers run. Then verify by running the code.\n\na) GET /a      b) GET /b      c) GET /c      d) GET /d\ne) What makes Express skip normal middleware and jump to errorHandler?\nf) Why does /d never reach errorHandler even though it 'looks' like an error?",
      "originalText": "For each request, write down the exact status + body the client gets\nand which handlers run. Then verify by running the code.\n\na) GET /a      b) GET /b      c) GET /c      d) GET /d\ne) What makes Express skip normal middleware and jump to errorHandler?\nf) Why does /d never reach errorHandler even though it 'looks' like an error?",
