    },
    {
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 36449,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 401004258,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795205146309,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "id": "e11",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 65,
      "y": 622,
      "width": 799.1999999999999,
      "height": 337.5,
      "text": "Instead of one giant errorMiddleware, split it into 3 error handlers\nregistered in order, in src/middlewares/:\n\n1. logError     -> console.error method, url, err.message; then pass it on\n2. translateError -> convert library errors into AppError:\n     - Mongoose ValidationError -> 400, message lists every field error\n       e.g. \"email: required, password: too short\"\n     - Mongoose CastError (bad ObjectId) -> 400 \"Invalid id: <value>\"\n     - err.code === 11000 -> 409 \"<field> already exists\"\n3. sendError    -> the ONLY place that calls res.status().json()\n\na) How does handler 1 hand the error to handler 2? (what exact call?)\nb) What breaks if translateError calls next() with no argument?\nTest: register with an empty body, a duplicate email, and GET a\nuser with id 'abc'.",
      "originalText": "Instead of one giant errorMiddleware, split it into 3 error handlers\nregistered in order, in src/middlewares/:\n\n1. logError     -> console.error method, url, err.message; then pass it on\n2. translateError -> convert library errors into AppError:\n     - Mongoose ValidationError -> 400, message lists every field error\n       e.g. \"email: required, password: too short\"\n     - Mongoose CastError (bad ObjectId) -> 400 \"Invalid id: <value>\"\n     - err.code === 11000 -> 409 \"<field> already exists\"\n3. sendError    -> the ONLY place that calls res.status().json()\n\na) How does handler 1 hand the error to handler 2? (what exact call?)\nb) What breaks if translateError calls next() with no argument?\nTest: register with an empty body, a duplicate email, and GET a\nuser with id 'abc'.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
