      "id": "e17",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 65,
      "y": 1129.5,
      "width": 777.6,
      "height": 270,
      "text": "This route sometimes crashes the server log with\n\"Error [ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT]: Cannot set headers after they are sent\".\n\na) Trace the flow when the file does NOT exist. How many times\n   does the code try to respond? Name each place.\nb) Trace when the file exists but JSON.parse throws. Does the\n   error reach the global handler? Why / why not?\nc) Fix the route (keep callbacks, no async/await) so every path\n   responds exactly once and errors go through next(err).\nd) Add a guard at the top of your global handler:\n   if (res.headersSent) return next(err)\n   Explain what Express's default handler does in that case.",
      "originalText": "This route sometimes crashes the server log with\n\"Error [ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT]: Cannot set headers after they are sent\".\n\na) Trace the flow when the file does NOT exist. How many times\n   does the code try to respond? Name each place.\nb) Trace when the file exists but JSON.parse throws. Does the\n   error reach the global handler? Why / why not?\nc) Fix the route (keep callbacks, no async/await) so every path\n   responds exactly once and errors go through next(err).\nd) Add a guard at the top of your global handler:\n   if (res.headersSent) return next(err)\n   Explain what Express's default handler does in that case.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aG"
    },
